  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-27378529" secondary-reporter="0" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Netherlands Enterprise Agency</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From feed to food: guaranteed consumer-safe feed production of dairy feed by means of a fully controlled feed production chain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on the innovative concept of an integrated chain approach. Besides ISO certification as a result, also audits and controls of raw material suppliers will be performed, next to the installation of a tracking and tracing system in Vietnam where the usage of antibiotic containing feed is nowadays common practice and carries the risk of unhealthy consumer foods, especially in the targeted product: milk.With this in mind, the applicant intends to establish the first fully controlled production chain and guaranteed antibiotic-free production line in Vietnam dedicated to only producing dairy feed. This production line will be fully controlled by a dedicated quality department, responsible for auditing raw material suppliers and the quality control of raw materials supplied. The norms and guidelines, under which the quality department will be working, will be based on the new quality standard and the CSR policy of De Heus International B.V. in the Netherlands.Local farmers will be trained on how to avoid the usage of antibiotics. These technical trainings will be provided in seminars and through on-farm advice to individual farmers. The training programme also includes training of technical staff, working for the company.</narrative>
  </description>
